# Safe template for optional bind-mount workflows with the new nvpn-client 0.9.x.
#
# Two valid workflows:
#
# 1) READ-WRITE bind mount + -e overrides (recommended for development):
#       cp sample-config.example sample-config
#       # leave UDID as the placeholder — docker-entrypoint.sh patches it at
#       # startup from -e UDID=...
#       docker run ... \
#         -v "$PWD/assets/sample-config:/etc/nvpn-client/config" \
#         -e UDID="$AGENTVPN_UDID" \
#         agentvpn daemon
#    The entrypoint will write UDID into the mounted file and strip any
#    leftover REPLACE_WITH_* placeholders before starting nvpn-client.
#
# 2) READ-ONLY bind mount with everything pre-filled (for locked-down envs):
#       cp sample-config.example sample-config
#       sed -i "s|REPLACE_WITH_DEVICE_UDID|$AGENTVPN_UDID|" sample-config
#       docker run ... \
#         -v "$PWD/assets/sample-config:/etc/nvpn-client/config:ro" \
#         agentvpn daemon
#    With :ro the entrypoint detects the read-only file and skips its
#    env-var patch step entirely (so any -e UDID=... would be IGNORED). The
#    mounted file must therefore contain the final UDID and any other values
#    you need; placeholders will reach Elysium and produce a 401.
#
# 3) Or skip the file workflow altogether and pass everything via -e flags;
#    the in-image config.template (placeholders only) will be used.

# Required: Agent VPN device UDID (sufficient for auth in 0.9.x).
UDID=REPLACE_WITH_DEVICE_UDID

# Optional overrides:
#ELYSIUM_AUTH_CLIENT_NAME=sprinkler
#VPN_SERVICE_BASE_URL=https://api.se-platform.com

# Optional cert pinning:
#ELYSIUM_CERT_PINS=fp1,fp2
#DISCOVERY_CERT_PINS=fp1,fp2

# Optional legacy client key (no longer required as of 0.9.x — leave unset
# unless your provisioning specifically issues one):
#ELYSIUM_AUTH_CLIENT_KEY=
